  "claim_scope": "OpenLORIS corridor1-1, 5000-image (2500-frame) and 10000-image (5000-frame) tiers, GT-free candidate generation/matching/mapping; ground truth used only for the post-map score in stage A4. This step reruns the old corridor1-1 base recipe (benchmark_electro.py --run --pair-source temporal-pyramid --rig-local-grouping) with --rig-frame-manifest added (arm D), a base-only rerun with no stereo8 bridge stage, to isolate the effect of the manifest flag alone from the diagnosed same-frame cross-sensor pairing failure. No GT-free stride-8 bridge is applied in this step -- the frontier this experiment characterizes is the base-only generalized_rig_sfm component frontier, exactly as in prior *-component-frontier-v1 steps.",
  "diagnosis": {
    "claim": "the old corridor1-1 base recipe (benchmark_electro.py --run --pair-source temporal-pyramid --rig-local-grouping, no --rig-frame-manifest) generated almost no same-frame cross-sensor candidates, for two independently confirmed reasons",
    "reason_a": "without --rig-frame-manifest, examples/unordered_sfm_demo.rs's rig_camera_timestamp (unordered_sfm_demo.rs:3257-3277) derives its grouping 'timestamp' directly from the trailing numeric suffix of the filename (e.g. cam1_000000.png -> timestamp 0, cam2_000001.png -> timestamp 1). Because this repo's cam1/cam2 filenames use disjoint even/odd numeric suffixes for the same physical instant, rig_local_pairs (used only when rig_local_grouping is actually active) never sees a matching (camera, timestamp) pair across sensors -- cam1 and cam2 frames from the same instant never collide.",
    "reason_a_verified_by": "read examples/unordered_sfm_demo.rs:3257-3277 (rig_camera_timestamp) and the surrounding rig_local_pairs doc comment directly; not re-run",
    "reason_b": "scripts/benchmark_electro.py's build_candidate_command only appends --rig-local-grouping to the launched command when pair_source == 'vlad-union' (benchmark_electro.py:1037-1038: 'if pair_source == \"vlad-union\" and rig_local_grouping: command.append(\"--rig-local-grouping\")'). For pair_source == 'temporal-pyramid' the flag is silently dropped even when the CLI wrapper was invoked with --rig-local-grouping.",
    "reason_b_verified_by": "read scripts/benchmark_electro.py:964-1038 directly (build_candidate_command); confirmed empirically in this same experiment's own artifacts below (reason_b_reproduced_in_this_run)",
    "reason_b_reproduced_in_this_run": {
      "claim": "even in this experiment's own run_d0.sh (which passes --rig-local-grouping on the CLI), the resulting candidate-generation.log effective-config shows rig_local_grouping: false for both tiers -- the flag drop is confirmed live, not just by reading source",
      "tier5000_effective_config_excerpt": "pair_source: TemporalPyramid, local_stem_window: None, rig_local_grouping: false, rig_frame_manifest: Some(\"/home/sasaki/datasets/openloris/m9-learned-retrieval-models-v1/openloris-tier5000-rig-manifest-v1.txt\")",
      "tier10000_effective_config_excerpt": "pair_source: TemporalPyramid, local_stem_window: None, rig_local_grouping: false, rig_frame_manifest: Some(\"/home/sasaki/datasets/openloris/m9-learned-retrieval-models-v1/openloris-tier10000-rig-manifest-v1.txt\")",
      "source": "pipeline-sparse7n/candidate-generation.log in both openloris-tier{5000,10000}-rigframe-base-v1 artifact roots",
      "implication": "this run's near-complete recovery of same-frame cross-sensor candidates (see results_per_tier below) is attributable entirely to --rig-frame-manifest; --rig-local-grouping contributed nothing in this run because it was silently dropped, exactly as reason_b predicts"
    },
    "verified_pair_pass_rate": "when same-frame cross-sensor pairs are proposed as candidates, they verify (pass geometric verification) at 92-100% in every tier examined",
