  "lead_analysis": [
    "1. The diagnosis is confirmed: adding --rig-frame-manifest alone restores same-frame cross-sensor candidates from near-zero (old: 1/1 at 5k, 111/111 at 10k) to essentially complete (new: 2500/2408 verified at 5k, 5000/4686 verified at 10k) and fixes rank-0 Sim(3) scale (5k 0.381 -> 1.0264 rank0 / new 2-component split; 10k 0.045 -> 0.9865 rank0), with no stride-8 probe stage of any kind.",
    "2. At 5k, base-only arm D reaches 2475/2500 frames (4950/5000 images) with aggregate RMSE 0.2686 m -- close to the previous best 5k configuration (gap46: 2484 frames) but without that configuration's degenerate rank-0 RMSE of 3.32 m.",
    "3. At 10k, arm D fails the pre-registered accuracy gates versus C' (Q2 RMSE 0.8879 m and p95 2.0204 m both far exceed the C'-derived thresholds; Q3 fails because component rank 2's sim3_scale 0.6495 is well outside [0.9, 1.1]), so C' remains the 10k development-tier configuration -- arm D is not adopted at 10k.",
    "4. Confound, not a claim: the per-component Sim(3) aggregate rewards fragmentation. Arm D's rank-0 component spans 6370 images (3185 frames) with drift growing along the trajectory (segment RMSE 0.16 -> 2.22 m over the last 5 of 10 segments), whereas C' splits the same trajectory into more, shorter, independently-aligned components. COLMAP's own 10k reconstruction likewise splits into only 2 components. A fragmentation-neutral metric (e.g. fixed-window relative pose error, not per-component Sim(3)) should be pre-registered before further D-vs-C' comparisons are drawn.",
    "5. The benchmark_electro.py silent drop of --rig-local-grouping for pair_source=temporal-pyramid (build_candidate_command, benchmark_electro.py:1037-1038) is a footgun: this experiment's own run_d0.sh passed --rig-local-grouping and it was silently ignored for both tiers (confirmed live in candidate-generation.log's effective-config, rig_local_grouping: false). The flag should either be forwarded for temporal-pyramid too, or the CLI should reject/warn when --rig-local-grouping is combined with --pair-source temporal-pyramid so future runs do not silently rely on a no-op flag."
  ],
